Body:
### Suggested Fix

The snapshot was introduced to isolate parallel tests from contaminating each other's env vars. However, this breaks runtime behavior where env vars may be set after initialization.

Looking at `packages/opencode/test/preload.ts`, tests set `OPENCODE_TEST_HOME` to indicate test mode. A simple fix would be to only use the snapshot in test mode:

```typescript
// packages/opencode/src/env/index.ts
export namespace Env {
  const state = Instance.state(() => {
    // Only create snapshot in test mode to isolate parallel tests
    // In production, read process.env directly to pick up late-set env vars
    if (process.env.OPENCODE_TEST_HOME) {
      return { ...process.env } as Record<string, string | undefined>
    }
    return process.env as Record<string, string | undefined>
  })
  // ...
}
```

This preserves test isolation while allowing runtime detection of env vars set after initialization.

Happy to submit a PR if this approach looks good.
